-- title:
--   Normalised Haar measure on a twisted centraliser, with orbital integral
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a finite Galois extension of $K$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by the integer powers of $\sigma$, and assume $[L:K]$ is prime. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion, let $\varphi$ be a function $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)\to\mathbb{C}$ that is locally constant with compact support, let $f$ be a function $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)\to\mathbb{C}$ that is locally constant with compact support, and assume $\varphi$ and $f$ are matching at $v$ in the sense of the predicate [`AutomorphicForm.AreMatchingOn`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L324) for $\sigma$ relative to the measures `semiLocalHaar` and `localHaar`. The assertion is: for all $a,t\in K_v^{\times}$ with $t\neq 1$ and all $\alpha,\beta\in (L\otimes_K K_v)^{\times}$, if the norm string $\delta\,\sigma(\delta)\cdots\sigma^{[L:K]-1}(\delta)$ of $\delta=\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta)$ (the product of the iterates of the $\sigma$-action `sigmaGL` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$) equals the image of $\mathrm{diag}(a,at)$ under the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ induced by $x\mapsto 1\otimes x$, then there exists a measure $\tau'$ on the twisted centraliser $\{x : x\,\delta\,\sigma(x)^{-1}=\delta\}$ of $\delta$, taken with its Borel structure, such that $\tau'$ is a Haar measure, $\tau'$ gives mass $1$ to the set of elements of that subgroup whose underlying matrix and whose inverse matrix both have entries in the image of `HeightOneSpectrum.tensorAdicCompletionIntegersTo`, and there exists $J'\in\mathbb{C}$ which is a twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi$ at $\delta$ relative to $\tau'$, in the sense of [`AutomorphicForm.IsTwistedWeightedOrbitalIntegralOn`](def/AutomorphicForm_WeightedOrbitalRelation.html#L53) for the measure `semiLocalHaar` and the weight `semiLocalWeight`.
--
--   This is the existence half of the local twisted weighted orbital integral datum attached to a diagonal element $\delta$ whose norm string is an exactly prescribed regular diagonal element $\mathrm{diag}(a,at)$, in the base-change comparison along the cyclic prime-degree extension $L/K$ at the place $v$; it supplies a Haar measure on the twisted centraliser normalised to give its integral points mass one, together with a value of the associated twisted weighted orbital integral. It is used in the local germ statement [`AutomorphicForm.exists_nhds_forall_eq_of_norm_sub_le_and_norm_add_halfWeighted_sub_le_and_forall_ratio_mul_sqrtRatio_mul_twistedWeighted_eq_of_areMatchingLocal`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_nhds_forall_eq_of_norm_sub_le_and_norm_add_halfWeighted_sub_le_and_forall_ratio_mul_sqrtRatio_mul_twistedWeighted_eq_of_areMatchingLocal), where it makes the relevant value well defined.
